---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/compare/"]}>
  <main id="main" class="ed-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <a href="/compare/">Compare EHRs</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">Compare Mental Health EHRs</span>
      </nav>
      <header class="ed-compact">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          Find the best mental health EHR for your practice
        </div>
        <h1>
          Start with the day
          <br />
          you want to have.
        </h1>
        <p>
          Your EHR is part of every visit. Choose one that helps you prepare,
          document, keep the record current, and get paid. We built Otto around
          the connections between those jobs.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="/demo/#watch">
          Meet Otto in two minutes ↗
        </a>
      </header>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Compare the options</span>
            <h2>See where Otto fits.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Use the same practice scenario in each product. Bring your
            must-haves and take the comparison beyond the feature list.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="resource-cards">
          <a class="resource-card" href="/compare/otto-vs-simplepractice/">
            <span class="tag">Comparison</span>
            <h3>Otto vs. SimplePractice</h3>
            <p>
              Evaluate documentation, practice workflows, and the terms you need
              to confirm.
            </p>
            <span class="text-link">Compare workflows ↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="resource-card" href="/compare/otto-vs-therapynotes/">
            <span class="tag">Comparison</span>
            <h3>Otto vs. TherapyNotes</h3>
            <p>Compare AI notes, claims workflows, and cost components.</p>
            <span class="text-link">Compare workflows ↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="resource-card" href="/tools/ehr-cost-calculator/">
            <span class="tag">Free calculator</span>
            <h3>Work out the full software cost</h3>
            <p>
              Include provider seats, AI usage, payments, claims, and setup.
            </p>
            <span class="text-link">Compare your costs ↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Why consider Otto</span>
            <h2>Follow the work through to the next step.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            Otto’s central idea is a connected practice day: useful context
            before the visit, documentation you review, and a clear path into
            the chart and payment.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>The context comes with you</h3>
            <p>
              Patient summaries and last-session highlights connect preparation
              to the documented history.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>The note moves the work forward</h3>
            <p>
              After signature, Otto proposes structured chart updates and
              carries the visit into charge review.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Clinical changes need your approval</h3>
            <p>
              Review the note, then confirm or dismiss the proposed diagnoses,
              plan items, and medication changes.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section">
        <div class="ed-section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Three useful questions</span>
            <h2>Choose for the work you repeat.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>
            The right fit depends on the patients you see, the way you document,
            and the services your practice needs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ed-facts">
          <section>
            <span class="tag">01</span>
            <h3>What happens after the note?</h3>
            <p>
              Follow chart updates, payment, and preparation for next time.
              Check where information carries forward and where you need to
              enter it again.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">02</span>
            <h3>Can you review and correct it?</h3>
            <p>
              Try the note editor, clinical approval controls, correction path,
              and record export. Understand how to recover when something needs
              attention.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section>
            <span class="tag">03</span>
            <h3>Does it fit the practice?</h3>
            <p>
              Confirm insurance, prescribing, paperwork, team access, migration,
              and costs. Evaluate the capabilities available to your account
              today.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-section ed-faq">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">A few useful answers</span>
          <h2>Get to know the details.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>
              What makes an EHR the best fit for a mental health practice?
            </summary>
            <p>
              Look for a fit with your actual visits: documentation format,
              clinical review, recurring scheduling, telehealth, billing, and
              record access. For Otto, evaluate the connected path from session
              preparation through approved chart updates and cash-pay
              collection.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Who should take a closer look at Otto?</summary>
            <p>
              Independent mental health providers interested in a connected
              workflow, particularly solo, self-pay practices. Discuss
              additional requirements with the team.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Where should I start if I am switching?</summary>
            <p>
              Begin with the <a href="/switch/">switching guides</a>. Inventory
              records, confirm the receiving workflow, test a sample, and plan
              continuity before changing systems.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="ed-close">
        <div>
          <h2>See what a connected practice day can feel like.</h2>
          <p>
            Watch Otto carry a visit from preparation through documentation and
            payment. Then tell us about the way you practice.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
          Join the waitlist ↗
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
